quran[13]{c,v,t}:
  27,64,"Or (ask them): ‘Who brings the creation into being, then returns it (to its former state)? And Who gives you provision from the sky and the earth? Is it another god besides Allah? Say: ‘Produce your evidence if you are truthful.’"
  27,65,Say: ‘No one in the heavens and the earth knows the Unseen (of his own accord) except Allah. And they are not (even) aware when they will be resurrected.’
  27,66,"Nay! Does their knowledge comprehend the Hereafter? No, they are just in doubt about it. Instead, they are blind to it."
  27,67,"The disbelievers say: ‘What! When we and our fathers become dust, shall we be brought out (from our graves alive)?"
  27,68,"We have indeed been promised this and our fathers before, but these are only myths of the ancients.’"
  27,69,"Say: ‘Travel in the land, then see how was the end of the guilty.’"
  27,70,"And (O Prophet!) Do not grieve over them, and do not be distressed for what they plot."
  27,71,They say: ‘When will this promise be fulfilled if you are truthful.’
  27,72,Say: ‘Perhaps a part of that (torment) you seek to hasten is close behind you.’
  27,73,"Indeed, your Lord is gracious to humankind, but most of them do not give thanks."
  27,74,And your Lord indeed knows well what their breasts conceal and what they reveal.
  27,75,"Nothing is hidden in the heavens and the earth, but it is (recorded) in a Manifest Book."
  27,76,"Indeed, this Qur’an recounts to the Children of Israel most of what they differ about,"
